## Slide 3

Event Definitions

## Slide 4

Event Definitions

Configuration
Represents configurable data entry fields to be collected during execution of a specific Event
An Event represents a span of time (typically a downtime) associated with a specific asset (System)
Configurable at the System OR Sub-System Level
A Discrete Trigger Tag property indicates when an Event Starts and Ends

Execution
Loaded and executed by the Logic Service
Events contain reference to related information, such Job, Batch, Product, Shift, OEE Type, and more.
When multiple downtimes occur at once, configurable rules will identify one as the primary cause for the Event record.

Packaging Line 1
Filler
Changeover
Jam
Tipped Bottle
Labeler
Jam
No Labels
Event Records
Event Definition

Available on Batch, Discrete and Storage Systems

