## Slide 19

KPI Calculations

## Slide 20

KPI Calculations

Configuration
Allows the collection of real-time production counts and event information to record Interval records in the TrakSYS Database
An Interval contains raw data over a timespan (typically 30 to 60 minutes) that can be used to calculate Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
Configurable at the System Level

Execution
Loaded and executed by the Logic Service
KPI Calculations contain reference to related information, such Job, Batch, Product, Shift, and more.
Standard TrakSYS has built-in TEEP and OEE aggregations and reports but can be extended to use variants 

Available on Discrete Systems only

