## Slide 23

Transfer Definitions

## Slide 24

Transfer Definitions

Configuration
Allows the real-time examination of an input condition to record instances of Transfer records in the TrakSYS Database
A Transfer represents a movement of a specific Material to or from a Storage System
Configurable at the System Level Only
A Discrete Trigger Tag property indicates when a Transfer Starts and Ends

Execution
Loaded and executed by the Logic Service
Transfers contain reference to related information such as Job, Batch, Product, Shift, and more.
Data records include captured information such as the Material Code and Quantity that is Transferred

Available on Storage Systems only

